From: alioth bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] alioth: poll CRC-checked FT5652 reports and deliver HID contacts

Opt-in alitouch=3 retains stage B power/setup and requires its CRC-valid
5652 identification before starting report polling. Stream 71-byte reads
through the 16-word FIFO with bounded RX/TX counts and timeout quarantine.
Validate CRC, status, IDs, event flags, count and raw coordinate bounds
before delivering ten possible contacts through existing SweetHID mapping.
Release absent contacts, tolerate transient invalid frames, release after
five consecutive invalid reports and keep polling with backoff. Limit logs.
No IC writes, firmware upload, DMA, GIC changes or partition operations.
Stages1/2 and existing console suppression remain available unchanged.
Physical report/HID behavior requires a full kernel build and device test.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_alitouch.h b/bsd/dev/sweet_alitouch.h
